Partial p11_L3_NPR33_20ms record, NPR 33, cold N2, L3, SST

Snapshot date: 2026-11-17. The solver remains running on 6 MPI ranks.
Last complete physical step captured in the current history: 192566 (not final).
Derived wall series is bounded at the last complete checkpoint: 192500.
Time step: 5.0e-8 s. Target: 200000 steps in this extension.
Last complete BDF2 binary restart pair: restart_192499.dat, restart_192500.dat.
Both were written on 2026-11-17 at 20:04 local time; the matching
restart_192500.csv also exists locally. No restarts are included in Git.

serie_partial.csv uses the run's step counter * dt, exactly as wall_series.py
does: local extension time through 9.625 ms. The nominal accumulated campaign
time is 10 ms + extension time, i.e. through 19.625 ms at this checkpoint.
This file is the p11 extension only; it is not concatenated with the earlier
10 ms campaign. The final extension will replace/complete this delivery.

The series was extracted using the repository's wall_series.py from a fixed
selection of wall files through step 192500. The raw wall files stay local.
serie_partial.png and trajectory_report.txt use wall_series_plot.py.
topology_L3.txt and tau_w_L3.csv use the repository's topology.py, selecting
the newest restart CSV by modification time.

STATUS, configuration files, log files and all history files are snapshots.
History/log files from interrupted attempts are preserved as produced; their
time ranges overlap after restarting, some histories contain shutdown damage,
and their Cur_Time resets on restart. Do not concatenate histories blindly.
Use the newest resume history for current health and the physical step counter
for the extension chronology. Missing ALL DONE in STATUS is expected while
the production run is active.
